 ${misc:Depends},
Description: Keel MariaDB, the database layer of Keel appliances
 The appliance manifest of Keel MariaDB (handbook decisions 0041, 0047 and
 0049), installed as /usr/share/keel/appliances/mariadb.yaml: Keel Core's
 five overlays inherited with their states, and the MariaDB server as the
 appliance's own process on 3306, a mesh port, with its Monit check, the
 db_password secret the first boot hook sets the administrative account
 from, and the db_user option that names that account.
 .
 With it a spec may say appliance.name: mariadb and declare the pair of
 docs/replication.md, a primary and a replica on the mesh whose primary
 holds the pair's VIP. It depends on keel-core 0.1.3, the first that
 carries the vip overlay, on keel 0.23.0, the first that configures such a
 pair, and on mariadb-server, whose unit the manifest names. Installing it
 enables nothing: keel spec apply sets each overlay to the state the
 instance spec gives it.
